WEBVTT

00:03.470 --> 00:06.874
Imperial Calendar Year 955

00:06.874 --> 00:11.412
As a result of the battle triggered
by the Triple Alliance's invasion...

00:11.412 --> 00:17.918
...the Humankind Abh Empire
began a huge retaliation.

00:17.918 --> 00:21.755
This retaliation was known as
Operation Phantom Flame.

00:21.755 --> 00:25.359
The Star Forces fleet of
Operation Phantom Flame...

00:25.359 --> 00:32.766
...has established a stronghold
in the enemy's territory.

00:32.766 --> 00:33.634
However, in response to
the Alliance's counterattack...

00:33.634 --> 00:36.704
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
However, in response to
the Alliance's counterattack...

00:36.704 --> 00:40.307
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...Operation Phantom Flame
has entered a new phase...

00:40.307 --> 00:41.075
...in which the objective is
to annihilate the enemy fleet.

00:41.075 --> 00:43.677
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
...in which the objective is
to annihilate the enemy fleet.

00:43.677 --> 00:45.379
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
They await the Triple Alliance
in the Aptic System...

00:45.379 --> 00:46.113
They await the Triple Alliance
in the Aptic System...

00:46.113 --> 00:50.413
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
...soon to be the main battlefield.

00:50.651 --> 00:51.085
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:51.085 --> 00:55.222
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:55.222 --> 00:56.190
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:56.190 --> 00:57.191
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:57.191 --> 01:00.327
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...the defense forces of Admiral
Bebaus consist of only twelve squadrons.

01:00.327 --> 01:01.128
...the defense forces of Admiral
Bebaus consist of only twelve squadrons.

01:01.128 --> 01:04.765
Aptic Defense Fleet Commander
Admiral Bebaus
...the defense forces of Admiral
Bebaus consist of only twelve squadrons.

01:04.765 --> 01:09.837
Given that they are outnumbered
by almost fifteen-to-one...

01:09.837 --> 01:13.603
...the two fleets have decided on
the time of the decisive battle.

01:18.312 --> 01:19.747
When I was a child...

01:19.747 --> 01:23.843
...we always played the same game
in the zero-gravity garden.

01:29.390 --> 01:32.292
To win the game, you had to knock
your opponent's lance away.

01:32.292 --> 01:35.557
It sounds easy, but it was rare
for a game to finish quickly.

01:37.598 --> 01:40.567
The players repeatedly launch
themselves at each other...

01:41.135 --> 01:43.504
...until eventually one of them
loses balance...

01:43.504 --> 01:46.496
...and the lance gets
knocked out of their hands.

01:51.545 --> 01:53.308
For some reason, this game...

01:53.747 --> 01:55.612
...was known as "jousting."

02:02.856 --> 02:06.314
The Flaming Battlefield

02:12.099 --> 02:16.934
Banner of the Stars

03:42.422 --> 03:43.190
You're leaving?

03:43.190 --> 03:43.557
The Humankind Empire Abh

03:43.557 --> 03:47.391
The Humankind Empire Abh
Yes, my term of office
is due to end shortly.

03:47.594 --> 03:49.830
I would like you,
as Prime Minister...

03:49.830 --> 03:51.832
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...to convey a message of farewell...

03:51.832 --> 03:54.630
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...to Her Imperial Highness
the Empress.

03:55.502 --> 03:57.371
I'm sure that won't be a problem.

03:57.371 --> 04:00.941
After all, the only country to have
maintained ties with us...

04:00.941 --> 04:04.536
...during the past three years
was yours, the Federation of Hania.

04:05.012 --> 04:06.413
Prime Minister...

04:06.413 --> 04:09.082
...our nation has avoided
establishing alliances...

04:09.082 --> 04:11.485
...with certain respectable nations...

04:11.485 --> 04:14.021
...since there is a war
that is already in progress.

04:14.021 --> 04:18.125
However, the fact remains that
we are still members of the...

04:18.125 --> 04:19.888
...Nova Sicily Treaty Organization.

04:20.427 --> 04:23.830
Imperial Prime Minister
Shidoryua Boruju Cid Seez
I'm well aware of that, Ambassador.

04:23.830 --> 04:25.332
Imperial Prime Minister
Shidoryua Boruju Cid Seez
But your country does act...

04:25.332 --> 04:29.036
...quite differently from the
other nations in the organization...

04:29.036 --> 04:32.199
...so forgive me if that alliance
happens to slip my mind at times.

04:33.006 --> 04:34.141
Ambassador of Hania
Guen Tauron
Oh?

04:34.141 --> 04:36.132
Ambassador of Hania
Guen Tauron
How do we act differently?

04:37.110 --> 04:40.581
The other countries...

04:40.581 --> 04:45.712
...have a tendency to trivialize any
differences in our political systems.

04:46.787 --> 04:47.854
However...

04:47.854 --> 04:49.957
...there is a vast difference
that has resulted...

04:49.957 --> 04:53.393
...in a gap between those
other countries and our Empire.

04:54.528 --> 04:58.232
Does this have anything
to do with you, a Lander...

04:58.232 --> 05:03.636
...wanting to achieve the
highest rank in the Empire?

05:04.671 --> 05:06.940
You could put it that way.

05:06.940 --> 05:08.208
However...

05:08.208 --> 05:10.438
...what do you think of this
for a reason?

05:11.612 --> 05:13.647
The power of this Empire...

05:13.647 --> 05:16.950
...is the only force that
can impose modernity...

05:16.950 --> 05:19.043
...onto the surface worlds.

05:20.120 --> 05:21.144
Do you follow me?

05:23.056 --> 05:25.991
I'm not sure what you're suggesting.

05:26.627 --> 05:28.060
Really?

05:28.562 --> 05:29.329
No.

05:29.329 --> 05:32.958
I suppose it would be wrong
for me to doubt you.

07:16.903 --> 07:17.838
Assault units!

07:17.838 --> 07:18.805
Pull back!

07:19.306 --> 07:21.274
Our ship, the Basroil...

07:21.274 --> 07:25.574
...was still in the middle of
a battle to defend the Aptic Gate.

07:29.616 --> 07:31.585
With the guard ships up front...

07:31.585 --> 07:33.487
...things are quite a bit easier on us.

07:33.487 --> 07:34.351
Yes.

07:34.788 --> 07:36.123
Did the ship suffer any damage?

07:36.123 --> 07:38.325
The armor plating was
hit in twenty-three places...

07:38.325 --> 07:40.894
...and there were small
pressure leaks in seven of those.

07:40.894 --> 07:42.953
But they've already been
taken care of.

07:43.864 --> 07:46.094
What about propulsion
and armaments?

07:46.299 --> 07:47.493
No problems to report.

07:48.034 --> 07:50.468
All personnel are alive
and accounted for.

07:51.338 --> 07:52.739
Thank goodness for that!

07:52.739 --> 07:53.671
Incoming message.

07:54.241 --> 07:56.143
All ships in the First Assault Unit!

07:56.143 --> 07:58.278
We are to make
a temporary retreat.

07:58.278 --> 07:59.973
Approval has been given
by battle HQ.

08:00.414 --> 08:01.176
No way!

08:01.782 --> 08:02.716
Commander!

08:02.716 --> 08:04.651
My ship can still fight!

08:04.651 --> 08:07.087
Deca-Commander Abriel...

08:07.087 --> 08:09.189
I'm afraid you don't understand.

08:09.189 --> 08:10.557
We can make a retreat...

08:10.557 --> 08:12.659
...precisely because
we can still fight.

08:12.659 --> 08:14.861
If you haven't seen
enough fighting, don't worry.

08:14.861 --> 08:17.159
We'll be back soon enough.

08:18.398 --> 08:19.422
I understand.

08:19.766 --> 08:21.165
That's good.

08:21.301 --> 08:23.136
If there are no more objections...

08:23.136 --> 08:25.338
...we'll begin to retreat
at maximum battle speed.

08:25.338 --> 08:27.397
I'll transmit the route information.

08:29.309 --> 08:30.143
Excuse me.

08:30.143 --> 08:30.905
Captain?

08:31.445 --> 08:32.776
Ah, yes...

08:33.480 --> 08:34.572
Retreat.

08:51.164 --> 08:52.461
The shame of it!

08:54.468 --> 08:55.366
Taste good?

08:56.770 --> 08:59.940
Maybe a nice cold drink
would be good right now.

08:59.940 --> 09:02.101
So I brought you one.

09:02.676 --> 09:05.167
But maybe you prefer
your own blood.

09:05.545 --> 09:07.848
What do you take me for?

09:07.848 --> 09:13.047
At times like this I can understand
how one might thirst for blood.

09:14.187 --> 09:15.552
Although I never feel that way.

09:16.256 --> 09:17.348
Me neither.

09:18.592 --> 09:20.760
So you weren't thirsting
for blood, after all.

09:20.760 --> 09:22.028
No!

09:22.028 --> 09:24.164
You don't have to deny it
so strenuously.

09:24.164 --> 09:25.188
Captain!

09:25.599 --> 09:26.733
Sorry to be so tacky, but...

09:26.733 --> 09:30.134
...can the crew get permission
to remove their pressure suits?

09:30.670 --> 09:33.073
The danger has passed
for the moment...

09:33.073 --> 09:36.209
...and working in those suits
can be fairly uncomfortable.

09:36.209 --> 09:37.836
Sorry, I didn't realize.

09:38.612 --> 09:39.412
Permission granted.

09:39.412 --> 09:41.175
Thank you very much.

09:42.115 --> 09:44.208
And what did you mean by "tacky"?

09:44.784 --> 09:45.318
Oh, nothing.

09:45.318 --> 09:47.343
It seemed like you two
were having fun back there.

10:10.610 --> 10:11.211
It appears that...

10:11.211 --> 10:15.113
...we severely underestimated the
number of mines the enemy had...

10:15.982 --> 10:18.652
The mine attacks are still going on?

10:18.652 --> 10:21.086
Such a senseless way to fight!

10:22.722 --> 10:25.592
I'd rather win senselessly...

10:25.592 --> 10:27.794
...than to lose because
we were being sensible.

10:27.794 --> 10:29.462
That goes for me, too!

10:29.462 --> 10:30.430
But right now...

10:30.430 --> 10:32.796
...we don't have much say
over how we choose to fight.

10:34.067 --> 10:36.467
Our patrol ships will
undoubtedly run out of mines.

10:37.537 --> 10:40.335
Give them permission to use
the electromagnetic cannons.

10:40.774 --> 10:43.470
Yes, I suppose that's the
most sensible response.

10:44.277 --> 10:46.079
Before you change your mind...

10:46.079 --> 10:48.114
...and come up
with some senseless idea...

10:48.114 --> 10:50.014
...I'll get that order out right away.

10:51.017 --> 10:54.578
Three hours until
the main fleet arrives.

10:55.622 --> 10:57.317
I hope we can hang on.

11:06.099 --> 11:09.694
Our forces still have
control of the Aptic region.

11:14.941 --> 11:16.543
The Fourth Fleet, going in
from the right flank...

11:16.543 --> 11:20.035
...can split the path between
Wimpel and Aptic.

11:21.448 --> 11:25.407
Once the enemy passes, Admiral
Kotoponi can close off that route.

11:27.587 --> 11:30.890
Admiral Rulef's Second Fleet,
heading in from the left...

11:30.890 --> 11:33.259
...has secured the Mystel Gate...

11:33.259 --> 11:35.921
...and is approaching
the Aptic Gate.

11:36.730 --> 11:38.960
Mystel will be safe now.

11:39.132 --> 11:42.590
Let Admiral Mulusafa know
that he can come out of hiding.

11:42.936 --> 11:45.005
As soon as he receives his orders...

11:45.005 --> 11:46.706
...the Mystel Defense Fleet...

11:46.706 --> 11:49.504
...will become the Seventeenth
Fleet of Operation Phantom Flame.

11:49.909 --> 11:50.898
Yes, sir.

11:52.979 --> 11:55.174
Looks like we'll arrive just in time.

11:55.782 --> 11:57.150
That reminds me...

11:57.150 --> 12:01.177
...we've got Viscountess Paryunu
stationed in the Aptic region.

12:01.788 --> 12:03.915
And the young Count Hyde.

12:04.157 --> 12:07.388
I hear they're both onboard
the same ship.

12:09.462 --> 12:12.399
I hope those two are still alive.

12:12.399 --> 12:14.734
If they were to die...

12:14.734 --> 12:17.532
...I don't think I would be
able to sleep at night.

12:25.078 --> 12:26.680
Hey, I'm not getting
anymore output!

12:26.680 --> 12:27.747
A little to the right.

12:27.747 --> 12:29.544
No, left! Left!

12:31.317 --> 12:32.318
You're not my mother, you know!

12:32.318 --> 12:33.720
Hey, hey!

12:33.720 --> 12:35.779
Take it easy on that.

12:36.523 --> 12:38.825
This engine room's
a delicate creature.

12:38.825 --> 12:41.885
Treat it like you are petting a cat.

12:42.228 --> 12:42.853
Okay!

12:46.399 --> 12:49.459
Anyway, please load
as much as you can.

12:49.669 --> 12:52.797
We don't know when we're
going to be resupplying again.

13:13.326 --> 13:14.520
Diaho?

13:19.332 --> 13:20.533
I'll get you out of there.

13:20.533 --> 13:22.330
Just sit still.

13:23.336 --> 13:25.438
You shouldn't wander around
too much.

13:25.438 --> 13:27.474
If the crew were to
abandon ship...

13:27.474 --> 13:29.635
...you might get left behind.

13:32.278 --> 13:33.747
Although...

13:33.747 --> 13:37.513
...I hope we never have to
abandon ship.

13:54.300 --> 13:56.102
In the same way that you,
as a princess...

13:56.102 --> 13:58.738
...have your responsibilities
to your subjects...

13:58.738 --> 14:00.573
...as an officer of the Star Forces...

14:00.573 --> 14:02.976
...I have my responsibilities
to my crew.

14:02.976 --> 14:04.410
The Princess.

14:04.410 --> 14:06.674
So much for doing her a favor.

14:07.680 --> 14:09.582
Have I really...

14:09.582 --> 14:11.846
...got what it takes to be
captain of this ship?

14:14.120 --> 14:15.451
You think so?

14:20.260 --> 14:21.158
No.

14:21.661 --> 14:23.822
I just can't trust your opinion.

14:25.031 --> 14:27.329
The situation is getting
more serious by the minute.

14:30.370 --> 14:34.238
It looks like the patrol ships
are running out of ammunition.

14:35.408 --> 14:36.773
Running out of ammunition?!

14:37.143 --> 14:38.878
But we were planning to...

14:38.878 --> 14:41.870
...save the electromagnetic cannons
until the enemy ships arrived.

14:46.019 --> 14:48.078
I can't believe this.

14:49.222 --> 14:50.723
What are we going to do?

14:50.723 --> 14:52.350
Haven't you got any ideas?

14:53.359 --> 14:55.088
We'll have to conserve.

14:55.829 --> 14:58.932
You don't seriously expect me
to order the fleet to do that?!

14:58.932 --> 15:00.058
That's humiliating.

15:00.800 --> 15:04.429
It's less humiliating than losing
ships because we ran out of ammo.

15:05.004 --> 15:06.406
Wouldn't you agree?

15:06.406 --> 15:07.974
I know.

15:07.974 --> 15:10.076
We'll issue an order forbidding
all ships...

15:10.076 --> 15:12.306
...from using electromagnetic
cannons against the mines.

15:13.413 --> 15:16.109
But that will increase the
burden on the guard ships.

15:16.516 --> 15:17.951
Nothing we can do about that.

15:17.951 --> 15:19.719
Once the enemy arrives...

15:19.719 --> 15:21.621
...the guard ships can pull back.

15:21.621 --> 15:23.316
They can then take a break.

15:24.057 --> 15:25.149
I suppose you're right.

15:26.292 --> 15:27.527
Commander!

15:27.527 --> 15:29.427
A large number of enemy ships
is coming through the Sord!

15:31.130 --> 15:34.395
Finally, the battle is about to
enter a new phase.

15:36.803 --> 15:39.405
Guard ships to retreat immediately!

15:39.405 --> 15:42.135
Well, did the enemy run out
of ammunition too?!

15:42.442 --> 15:43.875
We're not talking
about the same thing!

15:45.245 --> 15:48.114
Even if the enemy
has used up their mines...

15:48.114 --> 15:51.017
...they still have plenty of
nuclear-fusion bombs.

15:51.017 --> 15:52.882
I know that, Nereis.

15:53.686 --> 15:57.349
Don't you think sometimes it's nice
to know you had the upper hand?

16:17.610 --> 16:20.841
This is the battle you've
all been waiting for!

16:25.852 --> 16:27.854
Mines and patrol ships...

16:27.854 --> 16:30.880
We've been dealing with
petty opponents so far.

16:31.824 --> 16:33.724
This time we're dealing with
enemy assault vessels!

16:53.913 --> 16:57.713
If any of you don't keep up,
I'll take it as a personal insult!

16:59.052 --> 17:00.853
I wonder if I'll ever be able to...

17:00.853 --> 17:03.515
...feel completely calm
during a battle.

17:05.425 --> 17:06.759
In any case...

17:06.759 --> 17:09.421
...we won't have to worry
about dormant mines any more.

17:09.996 --> 17:10.930
Yes.

17:10.930 --> 17:12.332
With the data from Command...

17:12.332 --> 17:14.300
...we're in a position
to identify them now.

17:14.600 --> 17:17.398
We can let the second aviator
deal with them.

17:20.606 --> 17:24.337
This is Captain Mooniju
of the 2107th Guard Fleet!

17:24.610 --> 17:26.679
We're under attack from
enemy assault vessels!

17:26.679 --> 17:27.737
Request backup immediately!

17:29.315 --> 17:31.017
All ships proceed at
maximum battle speed!

17:31.017 --> 17:33.747
Cut off the enemy fleet
from the guard ships!

17:35.054 --> 17:36.453
Main engine, full power!

17:42.395 --> 17:43.429
There are six enemy ships.

17:43.429 --> 17:45.198
We're at a disadvantage,
but it can't be helped.

17:45.198 --> 17:47.600
We'll identify the enemy ships
from right as enemies one through six.

17:47.600 --> 17:50.370
We all attack enemy six first.

17:50.370 --> 17:53.573
And then turn around
and attack enemy one!

17:53.573 --> 17:54.130
Yes, Commander!

17:54.741 --> 17:58.108
The enemy is in a cluster formation
with enemy six in the middle!

17:58.945 --> 17:59.969
Fire!

18:09.288 --> 18:11.257
Enemy six successfully destroyed!

18:11.257 --> 18:12.952
We're about to go through
the debris field!

18:15.428 --> 18:17.230
Ship's temperature rising!

18:17.230 --> 18:18.398
Still rising!

18:18.398 --> 18:20.195
A danger of armor meltdown!

18:20.600 --> 18:22.235
Do something about it!

18:22.235 --> 18:23.536
Do what?

18:23.536 --> 18:27.438
Increase cooling capacity
in all systems by fifty percent!

18:27.740 --> 18:30.476
Three... two... one.

18:30.476 --> 18:31.272
We've passed through!

18:32.145 --> 18:33.134
Come about!

18:40.987 --> 18:42.420
Lafiel! We're too far away!

18:48.127 --> 18:51.096
Well, the enemy ships
have turned around as well!

18:52.131 --> 18:54.497
That means they want to
continue fighting!

18:54.700 --> 18:56.793
Everyone, hang in there!

18:57.170 --> 18:59.968
Our next target is enemy one!

19:06.212 --> 19:07.577
Main engine! Ignite!

19:21.394 --> 19:23.362
When I was a child...

19:23.362 --> 19:25.387
...I wondered why jousting
was such a fun game.

19:26.232 --> 19:28.134
It must all be because of this.

19:28.134 --> 19:30.864
The enemy is approaching again
in cluster formation.

19:31.337 --> 19:32.672
Calling all ships.

19:32.672 --> 19:35.800
Our goal is to reduce their numbers
so that we're on an even footing.

19:36.409 --> 19:38.878
If we can't do that,
we'll have to retreat.

19:38.878 --> 19:39.367
Understand?

19:39.946 --> 19:42.380
If we don't end up retreating,
we set our sights on enemy three.

19:45.351 --> 19:48.621
The unit commander can be
surprisingly cautious.

19:48.621 --> 19:50.123
I feel relieved.

19:50.123 --> 19:51.556
What did you expect?

19:51.791 --> 19:53.259
Because we struck first...

19:53.259 --> 19:55.528
...we were able to go from four-
against-six to four-against-five.

19:55.528 --> 19:57.689
We need at least that
to take them on.

19:57.964 --> 20:00.066
If we lose and it becomes
three-against-five...

20:00.066 --> 20:01.397
...we wouldn't stand a chance.

20:02.502 --> 20:03.662
You're right.

20:04.237 --> 20:05.829
Enemy approaching!

20:11.644 --> 20:14.306
The enemy ships appear
to be targeting the Gamroil!

20:15.781 --> 20:16.509
Fire!

20:26.559 --> 20:28.151
Use the laser cannons!

20:33.900 --> 20:34.696
Where's the Gamroil?!

20:38.404 --> 20:39.701
We're fine.

20:40.473 --> 20:41.774
There's a change in plan!

20:41.774 --> 20:43.042
Target your attack on enemy one!

20:43.042 --> 20:44.236
We're going to finish it off!

20:44.677 --> 20:46.235
I want all ships to turn around!

20:51.350 --> 20:52.418
Captain!

20:52.418 --> 20:53.715
The engines can't take this!

20:54.120 --> 20:55.922
Let it rest after the battle!

20:55.922 --> 20:56.786
Okay!

20:56.956 --> 20:57.490
Captain!

20:57.490 --> 20:59.924
Enemy one is retreating
toward the Aptic Gate!

21:00.526 --> 21:04.428
Looks like we caused more
damage than we thought!

21:04.964 --> 21:06.999
Now it's four-against-four.

21:06.999 --> 21:08.134
Another change in plan!

21:08.134 --> 21:10.169
We're going to take out
enemy three!

21:10.169 --> 21:11.370
It is my firm belief that...

21:11.370 --> 21:14.999
...the Star Forces cannot lose when
matched up with equal numbers!

21:15.374 --> 21:16.898
And certainly not my squadron!

21:17.476 --> 21:18.841
And not my ship!

21:34.927 --> 21:36.326
Come about!

21:42.902 --> 21:46.906
We're all starting to
run out of fuel and ammunition.

21:46.906 --> 21:49.809
If we can't destroy enemy three
in the next attack...

21:49.809 --> 21:51.377
...then we'll have to retreat.

21:51.377 --> 21:52.211
Understood?

21:52.211 --> 21:54.008
Don't hesitate in pulling out.

21:54.580 --> 21:55.740
I'm not running away.

21:58.484 --> 21:59.451
Lafiel...

22:00.253 --> 22:01.345
Enemy ships approaching!

22:04.190 --> 22:05.282
I've never...

22:06.325 --> 22:09.817
...I've never lost in jousting!

22:29.248 --> 22:30.510
You going to fire at me?!

22:31.584 --> 22:33.848
All personnel! Brace for attack!

22:45.665 --> 22:52.833
Arrival of the main fleet...
one hour to go.

22:54.273 --> 22:57.834
kizukanai koto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.278 --> 23:02.941
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.717 --> 23:08.278
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.622 --> 23:13.388
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.559 --> 23:15.828
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.828 --> 23:19.025
haritsumeta kimochi ga
This tense feeling

23:21.033 --> 23:26.339
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keep facing forward

23:26.339 --> 23:29.365
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:30.276 --> 23:33.677
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.714 --> 23:39.185
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:39.185 --> 23:46.459
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.459 --> 23:51.630
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.630 --> 23:59.628
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.274 --> 24:07.446
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.446 --> 24:12.485
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our linked hands and our finger tips

24:12.485 --> 24:20.551
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.427 --> 24:25.557
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:31.537 --> 24:33.472
Do you want us to just sit here...

24:33.472 --> 24:37.465
...and wait while the enemy goes
ahead and destroys us, Nefee?

24:37.777 --> 24:39.267
Where do you think you're going?

24:40.546 --> 24:44.216
It would be a great dishonor to
know that I'd let my men die in vain.

24:44.216 --> 24:47.413
At the very least I would like
to choose where I end my life.

24:47.887 --> 24:50.754
Permission granted to take
any action necessary!

24:56.695 --> 24:57.863
All crew! Abandon ship!

24:57.863 --> 25:00.798
Next Episode...
The Battle for Aptic Gate Begins
